 ",[18,1722,352],{},[18,1724,356],{},[18,1726,1727],{},"Closer"," and more. Most functions accept ",[18,1730,20],{},", so passing ",[18,1733,1714],{}," works.",[1034,1736,1737,1620,1742,1594,1744,1746,1747,1631],{},[1477,1738,1739,1741],{},[18,1740,360],{}," is expected",[18,1743,489],{},[18,1745,360],{}," is normal end-of-input, not an error. Distinguish it from real errors: ",[18,1748,1749],{},"if err != nil && err != io.EOF { return err }",[1034,1751,1752,1757,1758,1760,1761,1763,1764,1767],{},[1477,1753,1754,1755],{},"File permissions on ",[18,1756,1461],{},": the third arg (e.g., ",[18,1759,618],{},") is the mode, applied after umask. ",[18,1762,618],{}," is user-rw, group-r, other-r. ",[18,1765,1766],{},"0600"," is user-only.",[27,1769,1771],{"id":1770},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[14,1773,1774],{},"A developer reads a file and processes lines, but the last line is sometimes missing:",[35,1776,1777,1947,1968,1971,2080,2089,2108,2112],{"language":37},[39,1778,1780],{"className":41,"code":1779,"language":37,"meta":43,"style":43},"scanner := bufio.NewScanner(f)\nfor scanner.Scan() {\n    line := scanner.Text()\n    process(line)\n}\n``\n::\n\nThey claim this misses the last line when the file doesn't end with a newline.\n\n\u003Cdetails>\n\u003Csummary>Answer\u003C\u002Fsummary>\n\nActually, `bufio.Scanner` **does** handle a final line without a trailing newline — `Scan` returns true for the last line and false after. This is correct behavior; the loop processes all lines.\n\nThe real \"missing last line\" bug is when using `ReadString('\\n')` with a `bufio.Reader`:\n\n```go\nr := bufio.NewReader(f)\nfor {\n    line, err := r.ReadString('\\n')\n    if err == io.EOF {\n        break   \u002F\u002F ❌ breaks before processing the last line if it has no \\n\n    }\n    process(line)\n}\n",[18,1781,1782,1794,1804,1816,1823,1827,1831,1835,1839,1851,1855,1860,1865,1869,1874,1878,1892,1896,1900,1905,1910,1923,1928,1933,1938,1943],{"__ignoreMap":43},[47,1783,1784,1786